AppServerSupport -- scoped launchd client

This framework supplies only the surface measured from the
CoreDeviceUtilities consumer: OSLaunchdDomain, OSLaunchdJob,
OSLaunchdJobInfo and OSLaunchdJobExitStatus.

Submission and removal use the existing ServiceManagement user-launchd
client. StartJob and job lookup use liblaunch's existing caller-UID
connection. Job state, PID, spawn error and wait4 status come from
fields the loaded launchd job actually reports; a failed lookup is
reported as an error, never as a zero-status exit.

Deliberate limits:

- The system domain is refused with ENOTSUP before submission. This
  client has no domain-correct system StartJob/GetJob route, so it does
  not submit into one domain and then query another.
- User and role-account domains for a different UID are refused with
  EPERM. They are not silently substituted with the caller's domain.
- StartJob-failure rollback is source-reviewed; no launcher failure
  injection was available, so it has no runtime injection claim.
- This is not a full native AppServerSupport implementation. It makes
  no native-equivalence claim and no claim that an application build
  succeeds. OSLaunchdJobProperties is not part of the measured surface
  and is not implemented.

The dylib carries its own current/compatibility version 1.0.0. The
consumer's LC_LOAD_DYLIB records current 3089.40.16 and compatibility
1.0.0; the SDK tbd's 3089.60.7 is metadata, not measured native runtime
provenance.
